  "annotations_dropped": [
    {
      "annotation_id": "ec27fca91d4c4ed58c6c30f24250cfe2_64",
      "summary_section": "issue",
      "labels": [
        "ISSUE"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:issue"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "On 01.06.2023, from the pleadings of the parties, following issues were framed :\n(I) Whether plaintiff is entitled to a decree of recovery of damages for a sum of Rs.10,00,000/-, as prayed for?"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "fab4e78032324cfb8d76e3abd2137cbc_65",
      "summary_section": "issue",
      "labels": [
        "ISSUE"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:issue"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "OPP. \n(II) Whether plaintiff is entitled to pendente lite and future interest at the rate of 18% per annum on the decreetal amount, as prayed for?"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "6ecfb9909f0a4e3095855bbc46ca7857_67",
      "summary_section": "issue",
      "labels": [
        "ISSUE"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:issue"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "In the counter claim, on 06.04.2021, on the basis of pleadings, the following issues were framed:\n(I) Whether the counter claimant is Jasvinder Singh vs Bharat Singh and Ors.\nBrij Sweets and Caterers vs Jasvinder Singh entitled for decree o"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "6b3dec74731e4c54b618c70dbb50c27d_112",
      "summary_section": "issue",
      "labels": [
        "ISSUE"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:issue"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "I find that the suit of the plaintiff has to be dismissed for the following reasons :\n(I) There is no corroborative scientific evidence to show that the dhokla sold by the defendant no.1 to the plaintiff was of a poor and adulterated qualit"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "26434c9093af4ed694be79956292eeda_115",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "It is pertinent to note that no such fact was ever mentioned in his evidence or in the plaint."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "90400a9055d64e9db6518a21e596b82d_116",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "No other evidence has been placed on record to show that the plaintiff made a 100 number call though the plaintiff has further deposed Jasvinder Singh vs Bharat Singh and Ors."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "e7a686eed5c04380a5d037107744b1ee_118",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "It has not been explained as to whether the said verbal complaint was made in person at the concerned P.S. or through a 100 number call."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "4191c3c7fc5b4ab4ad1932ce73acfe28_119",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "As such, the said cross examination shakes the credibility and veracity of this witness."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "2416e5e914dc4f4695169d9917a3d082_122",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": ". If the plaintiff was well enough to go to the shop of defendant no.1, then surely he would have been able to follow his complaint with Delhi Police, especially when he has also deposed that the Delhi Police, in fact, came at the time when"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "afb6271f26dc44af8e8787477f6cc555_123",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The plaintiff has not attempted to produce any corroborative evidence to show the involvement of police."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "91b79186895e42fb922e81bca082945c_127",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "This fact has cropped up in the cross examination for the first time and further damages the veracity of the plaintiff."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "5ff37b27766940e3b22b45e957ad8ebd_128",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "If indeed the police had played such a role, then it is hard to believe that the plaintiff would have omitted to say so in his plaint."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "18d574055de14bbf93f9ee89008741cb_129",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The plaintiff does not appear to be an illiterate or unaware person."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "da1d6fbd97ff43a48c3f61447b4388e3_130",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "He has impleaded not only the Food and Safety Department but also the Delhi Medical Council."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "9c6ca67c78f14b1d880e600e74f4e77d_131",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "He seems to be well aware about the role and functioning of the different authorities."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "33c243a1bb834ad49ca635b58f9cff95_132",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "If the Delhi Police had appeared at the spot and thrown away, what would be otherwise valuable evidence in the form of the remaining dhoklas, then the plaintiff would have surely raised a hue and cry about the same."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "01e62acff8e3464ea64a35c6c57a4137_133",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\n(V) In his affidavit of evidence, it is narrated by the plaintiff that immediately on taking one small piece of dhokla, he lost consciousness whereas during his cross examination, he has deposed that he did not become unconscious immediate"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "cd1ce09e1ead49f1ada24551a3589531_134",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "This again, is a material contradiction in his Jasvinder Singh vs Bharat Singh and Ors."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "b9754e54b2b54091820f9d061e1b9a64_135",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\nBrij Sweets And Caterers..Through ... vs Jasvinder Singh on 26 April, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/32787589/\n8"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "6cc952d81c934beba3f8d297086cf1ea_136",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Brij Sweets and Caterers vs Jasvinder Singh story."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "bf95c09ad37441bbaede062869953e37_137",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "As per his story, after he became unconscious, he was rushed to the nearest doctor by Sh. Sada Ram and his advocate Jai Prakash."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "5e5e8f4480e241089cc104e3277addd2_138",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "At this stage, a perusal of Ex.PW-1/2 which is the prescription issued by defendant no.2 would show that it is nowhere mentioned that the plaintiff i.e. the patient had been rendered unconscious."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "3a6a6a613bfc43e3b59b62c0e5450f0b_139",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "It has only been mentioned that he has complained of 'ghabrahat'."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "dbc187419b5249a788d365f944f2ce76_140",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "During the cross examination, the plaintiff had also deposed that after eating half piece of dhokla, he started feeling nauseous and after 10 minutes, he vomited."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "e2762267baaf41a6bdbc16e8ff707d9e_141",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The fact of vomiting would naturally, in the ordinary course of events, have been mentioned before the doctor as he was examined soon after the incident as per the story put forward."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "3b012f80d1ee49cd85fb5733c34e50a5_142",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "It is unlikely that such fact would not have been mentioned by the said doctor."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "12130ee92c8940f0bcbb6fd1db74ee7d_143",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\n(VI) In this regard, it may also be mentioned that the plaintiff cast aspersions on the treatment given to him by defendant no.1 i.e. Dr. Sumitra."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "e1bffa37437746efa77dcb0c388602b1_144",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "It is deposed by him that he approached a doctor at Ram Manohar Lohia Hospital, who informed him that the pain in his hip was due to the inefficient way in which he was given an injection by the defendant no.2."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "0bd673dd4fee41d3b69b2fe30b2a640c_145",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "No such evidence has been produced by the plaintiff."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "86b18b11cac745b89fd99dd6bf71a216_146",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The alleged doctor of Ram Manohar Jasvinder Singh vs Bharat Singh and Ors."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "3cc70941426340b5b8613a8899a7d570_147",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Brij Sweets and Caterers vs Jasvinder Singh Lohia Hospital has not been examined, nor has the prescription of the said doctor been duly proved."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "723c7ac92d7342c1af8d21b3ee7bebdf_148",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "There is no evidence to show that in fact, the plaintiff as administered any injection by defendant no.2."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "8c6efa9604d94c1fbfc9969a46a7436d_149",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The plaintiff has not even produced any medical expert who could depose about the injection given on the basis of the prescription given by Dr. Sumitra, which was exhibited as Ex.PW-1/2."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "67e3d05a02924e29b5d20998d91e03c6_150",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\n(VII) In so far as the liability of defendants no.3,4 and 5 is concerned, it is apparent that there is no master-servant relationship between the Food and Safety Department / MCD and defendant no.1,\nwho is running a sweet shop."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "86b590bb6237468ebb647e05229ca23e_151",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "At most, they are market regulators but can not be made liable for any deficiency in service by the service providers regulated by them."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "66b592df53fc40d1a25330831c15ed75_152",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "They have no direction or control over the activities of the defendant no.1."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "5d93177d29564f1b8d328dff91d76e7e_153",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Similarly, there is no master-servant relationship between the Delhi Medical Council and the defendant no.2 or for that matter, any other doctor who is a registered medical practitioner."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "7f23436f348442be9b2158adc529a079_154",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The DMC is merely a regulatory authority, who can not be made liable for any alleged negligence by a particular doctor."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "a26dc0e9e2fa44fda5a27f526f56fe16_155",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Moreover, it has also come on record that the plaintiff did not make any complaint to defendant no.5 about the alleged Jasvinder Singh vs Bharat Singh and Ors."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "82736a2e507646da81895d1682822c29_156",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\nBrij Sweets and Caterers vs Jasvinder Singh negligent service of defendant no.2."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "5026f0ded1af4317bb1b3c2261c3da92_157",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "This further shows that the claim of the plaintiff is lacking bona fides."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "0d2a28f2dfec48f1943f17050bb9a2ed_158",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "(VIII)"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "776eb4dfe6e140bfa0c8b6b000118f05_159",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The plaintiff has also not disclosed to the court that he had approached the Delhi Govt. Mediation and Conciliation Centre with his claim prior to filing the present suit."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "afb11e35e68649c8ba5236b29ed2186b_160",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The same was first brought on record by the defendant no.1 and admitted by the plaintiff only during his cross examination that he had filed a case for Rs.80,000/- in the Delhi Govt. Mediation and Conciliation Centre against defendant no.1."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "6ea12d7029d245e0936618fcf384306b_161",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The record of the Delhi Govt.\nMediation and Conciliation Centre and the complaint given by the plaintiff"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "6a27f51cde15413bb424b71ab78b15c3_162",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "where entered into evidence Ex. PW-1/C."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "0a7ff659df6e4cc3ba109a8dee84c132_163",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "This fact further ensures that an adverse inference will have to be drawn against the plaintiff."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "d137152048a34d37912c511165138dc6_164",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "In the complaint given by the plaintiff before the aforesaid Mediation Centre,\nno mention is made that he had become unconscious."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "5422d6aee3754bde979d3ef9a563e988_165",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Rather, it is stated that the plaintiff had developed fever, vomiting, stomach ache and loose motions."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "056ee388244c4c9ca1f0cc3babab034b_166",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The plaintiff has furthermore stated Brij Sweets And Caterers..Through ... vs Jasvinder Singh on 26 April, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/32787589/\n9"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "0f4dd5c3b294442dab2167318282dfd6_167",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "that he could not work for 15 days and had to spend Rs.80,000/- for his treatment."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "7d85630043344e54b7642587ef48a802_168",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The plaintiff has not proved even the expenses of Rs.80,000/-, let alone the sum of Rs.10,00,000/- claimed by him."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "63bda4cede4b45f3b87ba0bc9f9bafbd_169",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\nThere is not a single bill to show that a sum of Rs.80,000/- were spent on Jasvinder Singh vs Bharat Singh and Ors."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "8a5c027cdac44cd4b8e083c8b257536b_170",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\nBrij Sweets and Caterers vs Jasvinder Singh medical treatment."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "078e7cc39684433d95aa0789ea557c6d_171",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\n(IX) No other witness has been produced to corroborate the story of the plaintiff."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "afdd7b6f38134d06a5e54d1ae94a1b5d_172",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "21. Therefore, the issues are decided against the plaintiff and in favour of defendant no.1."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "1942789ab9474cb9a47d54b6e23f404d_173",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "FINDINGS IN THE COUNTER CLAIM 22."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "81e041f2aa0a4385b9c62a50155fc635_174",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The counter-claim has been filed on account of damages caused to the defendant no.1 due to the statements made by the plaintiff qua the quality of the dhoklas being sold by defendant no.1."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "3b24969346c94e9da07dc63db8f56796_175",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "It is claimed that the defendant no.1 has suffered loss to his reputation, respect and image in the locality of Qutub Vihar due to the publication made in the locality by the plaintiff qua the inferior quality of dhoklas being sold by defen"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "3c2ac04fe3164c74afa1215e8d4f8296_176",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "It is stated that defendant no.1 is conducting his business since more than 20 years and no such complaint has been received."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "c15139b22bbc4b6fb36f7bb22d2bf583_177",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "On this account, damages are claimed."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "86b46096e7cf42869c3485d28c7a1a8c_178",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "23. Before delving into the facts of the present case, it would be of benefit to recapitulate the law of defamation."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "74f1dab5932148bc8d8e3158f4a2def9_179",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "In Prof. Imtiaz Ahmad v. Durdana Zamir 2009 SCC OnLine Del 477 : (2009) 109 DRJ 357 the Hon'ble High Court of Delhi has held that:\nJasvinder Singh vs Bharat Singh and Ors.\nBrij Sweets and Caterers vs Jasvinder Singh \""
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "d03a3c9b8cb14741836addf010679d07_180",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "......Under law of defamation, the test of defamatory nature of a statement is its tendency to incite an adverse opinion or feeling of other persons towards the Plaintiff."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "f0c40b114ddb4169aac8098435aaa586_181",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "A statement is to be judged by the standard of the ordinary, right thinking members of the society at the relevant time."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "7ac9d0d7484b4266874b8ca7b41f3f0e_182",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\nThe words must have resulted in the Plaintiff to be shunned or evaded or regarded with the feeling of hatred, contempt, ridicule, fear, dislike or dis- esteem or to convey an imputation to him or disparaging him or his office, profession, "
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "50e1e844ca064739a0f2eca241e1ee7b_183",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The defamation is a wrong done by a person to another's reputation."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "ab44890d3714443b85d091de73fcdc44_184",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Since,\nit is considered that a man's reputation, in a way, is his property and reputation may be considered to be more valuable than any other form of property."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "18e945843b344a7e80cd1c9710c28fc8_185",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Reputation of a man primarily and basically is the opinion of friends, relatives, acquittance or general public about a man."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "54676a3d71c0458192991d33bb140962_186",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "It is his esteem in the eyes of others."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "d02b5390e3cd4adba66b8462280a7cf6_187",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The reputation spread by communication of thought and information from one to another."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "a05de24d9a73436ba6047eff7b3b0736_188",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Where a person alleges that his reputation has been damaged, it only means he has been lowered in the eyes of right thinking persons of the society or his friends/relatives."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "0bef15aebd154c58b0298d4ea0acaa02_189",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "It is not enough for a person to sue for words which merely injure his feeling or cause annoyance to him."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "1a50b56a7fd64feb88b329d0a9e4bed3_190",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Injury to feeling of a man cannot be made a basis for claiming of Brij Sweets And Caterers.."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "8f094a45e1004fd4a2c7215cd3ef2bde_191",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Through ... vs Jasvinder Singh on 26 April, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/32787589/\n10 damages on the ground of defamation."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "00aac83636cf4870a8d808d0206a13c9_192",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Thus, the words must be such which prejudice a man's reputation and are so Jasvinder Singh vs Bharat Singh and Ors."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "9c8733803f1d4b3c9f1188fd895f0222_193",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\nBrij Sweets and Caterers vs Jasvinder Singh offensive so as to lower a man's dignity in the eyes of others."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "948f0cdd49b94878a2912fc81a070043_194",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Insult in itself is not a cause of action for damages on the ground of defamation."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "fbcac91be1a744579a58816ee0798c30_195",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\n8. Where the words are used without giving impression of an oblique meaning but the Plaintiff pleads an innuendo, asking the Court to read the words in a manner in which the Plaintiff himself understands it, the Plaintiff has to plead that"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "7f3185fab0d947bd89cf6c0bad312690_196",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "24. In Brig. B.C. Rana v. Ms. Seema Katoch & Ors 2012 SCC OnLine Del 5421 : (2013)\n198 DLT 35, it was held by the Hon'ble High Court of Delhi that:\n\"......As a principle of equity, every man is entitled to have his reputation preserved inta"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "3124ed74ef564947a8e77b0f40c464c1_197",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "A man's reputation is his property and possibly more valuable than other properties, and any words calculated to cause harm to his reputation affords a good cause of action."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "385a8c1a9d7a4fdaa9a31b1fbdf921c3_198",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "21. Odger says in his book on Defamation that \"No man may disparage or destroy the reputation of another."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "6281a7f098a94e6fb56b1bef8436e9da_199",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Every man has a right to have his good name maintained unimpaired."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "077976f9eea847ddb22fa00ce1748cd4_200",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Words which produce, in any given case, appreciable injury to the reputation of another are called defamatory, and defamatory words Jasvinder Singh vs Bharat Singh and Ors. Brij Sweets and Caterers vs Jasvinder Singh if false are actionable"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "af347d9e939c4455bc46dc8854fb4eed_201",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "22. In Miller v. Thompson 1874 LR 9 CP 118, attempt is made to define defamation as exposing a person to contempt, ridicule, or public hatred or to prejudice him in the way of office, profession or trade."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "8cca99ed58e04829964fba5cacae8844_202",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\n23. Blackburn and George, in their Elements of Law of Torts, define defamation as a tort of publishing a statement which tends to bring a person into hatred, contempt or ridicule, or to lower his reputation in the eyes of right-thinking me"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "c21b29547eca4f909c87ec751d6db886_203",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "24. Faulks Committee in England in 1875 defines Defamation as \"Defamation shall consist of the publication to the third party of matter which in all circumstances would be likely to affect a person adversely in the estimation of reasonable "
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "6db6ad38eacb4d98a87bf611a9bc0f25_204",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\n25. To claim that a particular statement is defamatory there should be publication to a third party and such publication should be of such a nature as is likely to cause appreciable injury to a person's reputation."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "d72ed5d8cfba449faac135351f237468_205",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Defamatory words, if false are actionable."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "ed05eb4ea6804e669859aff97320eb53_206",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "False defamatory words, if written and Brij Sweets And Caterers..Through ... vs Jasvinder Singh on 26 April, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/32787589/\n11 published, constitute a libel, if spoken, a slander."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "3984298e2201461d994a17cfc6831093_207",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "In libel, the defamatory statement is made in some permanent and visible form in writing or otherwise recorded, such as, printing, typing, pictures,\nphotographs, caricatures, effigies."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "5945eb1138e9444a9bae2d9120b8facc_208",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "In Jasvinder Singh vs Bharat Singh and Ors."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "d585f75b9723457bafdbf8ddeed4da3c_209",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\nBrij Sweets and Caterers vs Jasvinder Singh slander"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "c7a0dfabac9d465a9ccda3278436ad0e_210",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": ", the defamatory statement or representation is expressed by speech or its equivalents, that is, in some other transitory form, whether visible or audible, such as, a nod, wink, smile, hissing, the finger-language of the deaf and dumb, gest"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "f9fddfef6c144a379d5a41a88bb86da2_211",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "26. In an action for libel the plaintiff should prove that the statement complained of (1) refers to him; (2) is in writing, (3) is defamatory, and, (4) was published by the defendant to a third person or persons.\"\n25."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "45e3f165178b4ca1a3aa0db4aa368b96_212",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The present counter-claim fails for the reason that there are no pleadings or evidence to show that any defamatory statement has been published or spoken to third parties by the plaintiff."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "644f7f3c4de84bc1b2b765d4937f07d7_213",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "RATIO"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\nMoreover, the defendant no.1 has not pleaded regarding the exact statement and words published by the plaintiff."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "8062c27d75e34a42adbc8ebd53baf4d9_214",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "RATIO"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "It is noteworthy that merely making such allegations in the suit filed before the court of law by the plaintiff would not constitute defamation."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "d5c7fe0087844c09abc99831a08daaac_215",
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "labels": [
        "RPC"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:decision",
        "forbidden_labels:RPC",
        "suspicious_label:rpc"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "26. Therefore, the issues are decided against the defendant no.1 and in favour of the plaintiff."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "23a41bf29878449ba3a47536f65c0794_217",
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "labels": [
        "RPC"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:decision",
        "forbidden_labels:RPC",
        "suspicious_label:rpc"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Therefore, the main suit filed by the plaintiff is Jasvinder Singh vs Bharat Singh and Ors."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "f3c8aebebf9d4de29b7b24042f83c811_219",
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "labels": [
        "RPC"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:decision",
        "forbidden_labels:RPC",
        "suspicious_label:rpc"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The counter claim filed by defendant no.1 is also dismissed."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "223355d6d6b64fb1bdf2fe88b8539a95_220",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "RATIO"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Before departing, it is also observed that the plaintiff has created a frivolous litigation and has impleaded multiple defendants such as the Delhi Medical Council, MCD, who could conceivably have had no relation to the alleged incident, fo"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "c6428a1c0c2043879562dc72b8869c51_221",
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "labels": [
        "RPC"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:decision",
        "forbidden_labels:RPC",
        "suspicious_label:rpc"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Therefore, the plaintiff is burdened with costs."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "f87272aefb6c4f1fabac26cf372a7870_222",
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "labels": [
        "RPC"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:decision",
        "forbidden_labels:RPC",
        "suspicious_label:rpc"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The plaintiff shall pay a sum of Rs.2,000/- to each of the defendants no.1 to 5."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "596039614f2840f0b922fa53721a38ae_223",
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "labels": [
        "RPC"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:decision",
        "forbidden_labels:RPC",
        "suspicious_label:rpc"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "He shall also bear the cost of his own suit."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "e187aaae1ad1449c8373f413717a3de9_224",
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "labels": [
        "RPC"
      ],
